  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Sign Out Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a sign out form?\", \"a\": \"A sign out form records someone leaving a place before the day is over, with the time and the reason. Schools keep one at the front office and another by each classroom door. Workplaces use one for staff who step off site during a shift.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you create a sign out form?\", \"a\": \"Choose the columns first: name, time out, destination and expected return, plus any check that has to pass before someone goes. Describe them to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, and it builds the form with a table of every exit. Then set it on a tablet where people leave.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a sign out form template I can start from?\", \"a\": \"Template sites offer printable sheets with the usual columns. A sign out form template has those columns but no rules, which means it cannot check a pickup list or time a hall pass. Describing your own form puts the rules in the first version. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing that form at a live URL.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a sign out sheet?\", \"a\": \"Draw a table with one row per exit and a column each for the name, the time out, where the person went, and the time back. Tape it by the door with a pen on a string. Paper works until someone forgets the return column, and nobody sees the gap before the end of the day. A form on a tablet stamps both times and shows which rows are still open.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an equipment sign out sheet track?\", \"a\": \"Record the item, its tag number, who took it, and when it is due back. A shared laptop cart or a key box needs one more column for the person who checked the item back in. Loans that run for days work better as a checkout form, which keeps each item's condition at both ends of the loan.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a bathroom sign out sheet include?\", \"a\": \"Keep it to the student's name, the time out, and the time back. A tablet version fills in both times and flags a pass after the limit you choose. The teacher spots a long absence at a glance instead of reading down a paper list.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a sign in and out sheet and a sign out form?\", \"a\": \"A sign in and out sheet logs everyone who enters a building, and the exit time closes each visit. A sign out form starts at the exit, for someone expected to stay who is leaving early. Built with Emergent, either one takes unlimited entries. Lobbies and job sites usually want a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/sign-in-form'>sign in form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the best place for a sign out sheet?\", \"a\": \"The spot where people leave: the front office for early pickups and the classroom door for hall passes. A paper sheet there shows every earlier name to the next person who signs. A tablet form shows only the blank entry, and the full log stays with staff.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who uses sign out forms?\", \"a\": \"Elementary schools use sign out forms when a parent collects a child early, and boarding schools add weekend leave. Service companies use them to see which technicians are out on jobs. The app Emergent builds has no per-seat pricing for the teachers and front desk staff who sign people out. Staff who will be gone a full day should file a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/time-off-request-form'>time off request form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a sample sign out sheet look like?\", \"a\": \"A sample sign out sheet has one row per exit, with columns for the name and destination, then the times out, and back. A school version adds the adult collecting the child. A workplace version adds a phone number for anyone working alone off site.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}